# Mobile / remote Cursor ops

Owner often edits from the **Cursor mobile app** while away from the PC. Treat mobile-sourced requests as **full desktop authority** over this repo.

## Do

- Edit any area the user names: engine, MetaAPI, protect/DCA, admin APIs, mobile UI, scripts, deploy configs, strategy tables.
- Prefer completing the asked remote change end-to-end (code → QA → commit/push/PR) without sending them back to a PC.
- When they say “everything / 다 / PC처럼”, cover the remaining product gaps in ordered slices, but **do not refuse** multi-surface work.
- Use admin `accountId` targeting APIs when changing another user’s MT5 account from phone.

## Still fail-closed (live money)

- Cases → risks → cost before trading-engine changes.
- Never force-close on API lag / partial orphan alone.
- Do not change open-basket logic mid-flight unless explicitly requested.
- No global sub-second polling of all accounts.

## Product surfaces for remote edit

- App: `/bot`, `/manage`, `/manage/strategy`, `/admin`, `/connect`
- Admin account picker + `?accountId=` / body `accountId` on strategy-bots/settings/bot/stats
- Engine/scripts under `scripts/` and `src/lib/meta-engine.ts`
